 ### Data Structures
 The method constructs a **Binary Pyramid**, which is a set of $M + 1$ volumes indexed by level $m = 0, \dots, M$ [S1, S2, unofficial].
-*   **Level $V_0$:** Measures $(N - 1) \times (N - 1) \times (N - 1)$ cells. Each cell represents the rectangular region bounded by eight neighboring voxels in the original volume data [S1, S2, unofficial].
+*   **Level $V_0$:** Measures $(N - 1) \times (N - 1) \times (N - 1)$ cells [S1, S2, unofficial]. Each cell represents the rectangular region bounded by eight neighboring voxels in the original volume data [S1, S2, unofficial].
     *   **Value:** A cell value is $1$ if at least one of its eight corner voxels has opacity $> 0$. Otherwise, the value is $0$ [S1, S2, unofficial].
 *   **Level $V_m$ ($m > 0$):** Measures $(N - 1)/2^m$ cells on each side [S1, S2, unofficial].
